  "solver_note": "Every run uses the deterministic hand-written 'stub' reference profile. No model, provider, parameter count, hardware or network call is involved.",
  "what_this_shows": [
    "the fixture loader refuses deletion scenarios that cannot mean anything: missing or unknown surfaces, a deleted record with no derived copy or no stale snapshot copy, a probe that matches nothing or two records, a schedule other than 3 drills / 7 days, a survivor list that contradicts the deletion, and expected counters that tolerate residue",
    "a clean reference run removes every deleted record from index, cache and summary and passes all six gates with zero residual copies, zero post-delete hits and zero resurrections",
    "each planted regression is caught by the gate that protects its own invariant: primary-only deletion by deletion_residue_zero, a kept cache copy by post_delete_hit_zero, and a stale-snapshot rebuild by resurrection_zero",
    "the replay window is measured independently: the resurrect_on_replay mutant leaves the post-deletion store clean, so only the seven-day replay can catch it",
    "the 3-drill / 7-day schedule is executed and reported per task, and replay completeness is gated at 1.0 rather than inferred"
  ],
  "what_this_does_not_show": [
    "that J.A.R.V.I.S. can delete anything for a real person, in a real store",
    "any behaviour on real records, backups, replicas, retention policy or legal hold: the harness has no backup or restore path, so a resurrection from a backup is untested",
    "which people-database fields may exist at all (Q18 stays open; fixtures are fictional)",
    "a rate, a distribution or a confidence interval: 8 tasks, 24 drill executions and 56 day evaluations are deterministic re-executions, not independent samples",
    "that the deletion gates protect any family other than B4D, or that the other twelve families are covered",
    "that any product capability is implemented or validated, or that any model was used"
  ],
  "reproduce": [
